    "created_at": "2015-06-10T22:55:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-06-10T22:56:56Z",
    "body": "I can make this smarter, but changes will of course change _other_ specs. But I doubt people really care, so I'm open to changing.\n\nThe problem is that if you have multiple overrides of a method, I need to have disambiguating IDs, so I took the conservative route and produced guaranteed-unambiguous IDs.  I can instead look for collisions and generate simple IDs when there aren't any.\n\nI was afraid that doing so would mean that the IDs would change if you added or removed an override, but right now they change if you change the arglist, which is more likely to happen, so I guess I'm screwed either way.  Might as well generate shorter URLs.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
